            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The petitioner contends that under the harmless\u2011error statute, courts must examine the error, its context, and whether the government can prove beyond a reasonable doubt that the error did not affect the jury\u2019s verdict."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 55,
              "start": 55
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The government argues that a rational jury would have found the defendant guilty despite the error."
      }
    ],
